# Per-instant Swiss Ephemeris longitudes, and the per-row tables that carry a
# Swiss column beside ours.
#
# RIGHTS.md's standing position is that Swiss output is used here as a
# MEASUREMENT and is not redistributed, which sidesteps the unsettled
# question of whether the AGPL reaches a program's numerical output. Bulk
# per-instant Swiss values are therefore not committed. What is committed is
# report.json, which carries only differences and summary statistics, and the
# instant lists, which are ours.
#
# Re-create these by re-running the harness against a local Swiss ephemeris:
#   node examples/precision-alpha/tools/measure/four-configurations.mjs \
#     --pack <pack> --kernel <kernel> --ephe <swiss-ephe-dir>
swiss-*.json
rows-*.json
